# Rule: adaptive_trust_threshold
# Category: Adaptive Thresholds
# Severity: high
# Attack Class: trust_degradation
#
# Adaptive detection: uses the ML anomaly_score together with the trust
# score to fire for agents that are both statistically anomalous AND have
# degraded trust.  This catches slow-burn attacks where either signal alone
# might not cross its threshold.
#
# Logic:
#   trust_score < 0.6   (below "healthy" but not yet critical)
#   AND anomaly_score > 0.7  (ML model flags anomaly)
#   → combined signal → high-severity alert
#
# The anomaly_score comes from the ML inference pipeline (Phase 2, Block J).
# The trust_score comes from the Rust Trust Graph Engine (Block K).

trust_score(event.agent_id, "agent") < 0.6
AND event.anomaly_score > 0.7
